  "created": "2026-11-14T16:41:56.043Z",
  "description": "1.8.0 - Consul crypto logic moved to shared Carbon.ConsulSecretEncryptor.Core (used by Console/Web tools). Consul JSON config supports whole-document (\"CarbonEncryptedConfig\") and field-level (\"ENC(...)\") encryption via AES-256-GCM+RSA-OAEP/SHA256 envelope, auto-decrypted on load and on reload-on-change. Consul HTTP Basic Auth support via CONSUL_BASIC_AUTH_ENCRYPTED.\n\t  1.7.0 - Consul ACL token support via CONSUL_ACL_TOKEN_ENCRYPTED, decrypted using a host cert (CONSUL_ACL_CERT_THUMBPRINT/SUBJECT). Consul watch traffic tunable via CONSUL_RELOAD_ON_CHANGE/CONSUL_POLL_WAIT_TIME_SECONDS.\n\t  1.6.1 - Replaced #if DEBUG check with runtime ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development check in UseFeatures.\n\t  1.6.0 - net10.0 target added; existing targets preserved.\n\t  1.5.1 - Carbon.Common version update.\n      1.5.0 - .NET 8.0 target added, older versions removed.\n      1.4.0 - Carbon.Serilog added; Serilog.Enrichers.Sensitive added for masking sensitive log values.\n      1.3.3 - Carbon.Common updated; IQueryable OrderBy extension bug fixed.\n      1.3.2 - Carbon.Common updated; nested ordering supported.\n      1.3.1 - Minor refactorings, typos.\n      1.3.0 - Multiple Consul support added; file config support for Kubernetes apps.\n      1.2.0 - Removed Serilog.Sinks.ElasticSearch (ElasticSearch.Net dependency conflict with ES 7.x); add it back manually if your app logs to ElasticSearch.",
  "id": "Carbon.ConsoleApplication",
  "isPrerelease": false,
